{"schema_version": 2, "model": "google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 100003, "k": 64}, "seed": 1314578831, "solved": "solved", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": true, "verify_reason": "ok", "reply": "To find the required coefficients \\( c(i,j) \\) of the polynomial \\( P(u,v) = \\sum_{r=0}^{p-1} (1+u)^r (1+v)^r \\pmod p \\), we can use the property of sums of polynomials over finite fields. The coefficient \\( c(i,j) \\) is equivalent to:\n\\[ c(i,j) \\equiv \\sum_{r=0}^{p-1} \\binom{r}{i} \\binom{r}{j} \\pmod p \\]\nThe product of the combinations \\( \\binom{r}{i} \\binom{r}{j} \\) is a polynomial in \\( r \\) of degree \\( i+j \\). Over the prime field \\( \\mathbb{F}_p \\), the sum of \\( r^k \\) for \\( r = 0 \\) to \\( p-1 \\) is \\( 0 \\pmod p \\) for any integer \\( 0 \\le k < p-1 \\). For \\( k = p-1 \\), the sum is \\( -1 \\pmod p \\). \nSince all given queries satisfy \\( i+j \\le p-1 \\):\n- If \\( i+j < p-1 \\), the degree of the polynomial is strictly less than \\( p-1 \\), yielding a sum of \\( 0 \\pmod p \\).\n- If \\( i+j = p-1 \\), the sum evaluates specifically to \\( (-1)^i \\pmod p \\).\n\nUsing this rule, we construct the coefficient vector \\( [c(i_1, j_1), c(i_2, j_2)]^T \\) for each block and multiply it by the provided \\( 2 \\times 2 \\) matrix. All arithmetic is reduced modulo \\( p = 101399 \\).\n\nFor example, in Block 0:\n- First query (1, 1): \\( 1+1 = 2 < 101398 \\implies c(1,1) = 0 \\)\n- Second query (39801, 61597): \\( 39801+61597 = 101398 = p-1 \\implies c(39801,61597) = (-1)^{39801} \\equiv -1 \\pmod p \\)\n- Column vector: \\( \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ -1 \\end{bmatrix} \\)\n- Output: \\( \\begin{bmatrix} 85385 & 100308 \\\\ 46719 & 47398 \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ -1 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} -100308 \\\\ -47398 \\end{bmatrix} \\equiv \\begin{bmatrix} 1091 \\\\ 54001 \\end{bmatrix} \\pmod{101399} \\)\n\nFollowing this through for all blocks, we obtain the evaluated vectors.\n\n<answ